WEBVTT

00:00.960 --> 00:05.840
Start by entering where the work is needed and choosing a suitable search distance.

00:10.240 --> 00:15.600
Describe the difficulty you want to address and Accessible Trades suggests relevant trade

00:15.600 --> 00:21.520
categories for you to review before searching. Compare nearby companies using details such as

00:21.520 --> 00:27.920
distance, supporting evidence and stated coverage. Switch to the map to understand where registered

00:27.920 --> 00:33.680
offices are located within the search area. Enhanced profiles bring useful company information

00:33.680 --> 00:40.160
together including services, recent work, supporting evidence, customer review summaries

00:40.160 --> 00:46.320
and practical project details. Contact options make it easier to continue your research directly

00:46.320 --> 00:59.120
with the company. The planning and support area also provides guidance for different stages of

00:59.120 --> 01:05.520
a home adaptation including an initial disabled facilities grant checker. Answer six simple

01:05.520 --> 01:11.120
questions to explore whether a disabled facilities grant route may be relevant. The checker does not

01:11.120 --> 01:17.040
ask for income, savings or medical details. The result explains whether the route may be worth

01:17.040 --> 01:23.040
exploring and highlights the next steps including a needs assessment, any applicable financial

01:23.040 --> 01:27.040
assessment and securing approval before work begins.

